From 71008d796be5c88857713a6afc0191643f415797 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:51:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FixedPointSolver: iterative solvers of the factory, None for
 the acceleration

Review of the NewtonK0 method:

- TangentLinearSolver and PredictionLinearSolver name an iterative solver
  of MFEM declared in the factory of the linear solvers (CGSolver by
  default, GMRESSolver, FGMRESSolver, BiCGSTABSolver, MINRESSolver,
  SLISolver), preconditioned by the linear solver of the elastic operator
  (ElasticOperator stays a synonym of CGSolver for the predictions). The
  conjugate gradient requires a symmetric positive definite tangent
  operator: this is documented, with GMRESSolver or BiCGSTABSolver for the
  other ones. FGMRESSolver is declared in the factory (variable
  preconditioners).
- Acceleration accepts None, so that an accelerated solver may switch to
  NewtonK0. Options given with None are refused.
- The preconditioners applying the linear solver of the elastic operator
  are removed before this linear solver is replaced; the correction solver
  is built in the protected block of the initialization.
- The documentation of NewtonK0 states that ElasticOperatorComputation and
  ElasticOperatorUpdate apply (EachResolution sets up the linear solver of
  K0 at each resolution).
- Anderson: the regularization must be greater than 1e-14, so that the
  regularized normal equations stay above the rounding errors.

Tests: NewtonK0 with each iterative solver, without assembly of the
tangent operator, with the prediction by the elastic operator, the number
of Newton iterations (up to one); options changed between the time steps;
prediction at constant gradients made by the linear solver of the problem;
new refusals. Six mutations of these fixes are detected.
